   "title": "\u2139\ufe0f About \u2014 Workflow Image & Versioning",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# \ud83e\udde0 BrainDead \u2014 Workflow Image & Versioning\n\nEverything in the pack that treats the **workflow itself** as data: snapshot it,\ndiff it, restore it, and render it as a shareable card with the graph embedded.\n\n## The problem these solve\nComfyUI's stock `SaveImage` embeds the full graph into every PNG. The BD save\nnodes write clean images with no metadata \u2014 good for delivery, but then nothing\nrecords how a render was made.\n\n## The provenance chain\n1. **BD_SaveContext** \u2014 registers naming + base dir for a run, and writes the run's\n   graph **once** as a native `.json` you can drag back in.\n2. **BD_SaveFile** \u2014 writes the product plus a `.json` sidecar. `embed_workflow`\n   (default **off**) also writes the graph into the PNG's text chunks.\n3. **BD_SaveWorkflowImage** \u2014 the human-readable card.\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f The one gotcha\nA node only receives the graph if the **client sends it**. The ComfyUI UI always\ndoes. A headless caller must post it:\n\n```json\nPOST /prompt\n{\"prompt\": {...},\n \"extra_data\": {\"extra_pnginfo\": {\"workflow\": <UI graph>}}}\n```\n\nWithout it the graph is `null`, sidecars record nothing, and saved PNGs will\n**not** open in ComfyUI."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
